job_description:
# Compliance Analyst - KYB

United Kingdom, London / Full-time: Remote / Compliance

Apply for this Job

Binance is a leading global blockchain ecosystem behind the world’s largest cryptocurrency exchange by trading volume and registered users. We are trusted by 300+ million people in 100+ countries for our industry-leading security, user fund transparency, trading engine speed, deep liquidity, and an unmatched portfolio of digital-asset products. Binance offerings range from trading and finance to education, research, payments, institutional services, Web3 features, and more. We leverage the power of digital assets and blockchain to build an inclusive financial ecosystem to advance the freedom of money and improve financial access for people around the world.

### Responsabilities:

- Act as a point of escalation and subject matter expert for Corporate onboarding cases;
- Ability to take on and lead special assignments and projects;
- Take the lead on adhoc QA checks to support the regional team;
- Identify and propose procedure and process enhancements;
- Work with the team lead and Manager for ongoing assessments, assisting with compliance reviews, and ongoing or ad hoc reviews;
- Work closely with MLRO’s, Account Managers/ VIP and other key stakeholders within the business;
- Proficiency in compliance applications and programmes such as Worldcheck etc;
- Good knowledge on provisions of local laws, directives, regulations and otherwise standards applicable to subject persons and knowledge of upcoming regulation of virtual currency policies is a strong plus;
- Good proficiency in conducting customer risk assessments, periodic/trigger reviews and enhanced due diligence;
- Identification and documentation of unusual activity or AML flags;
- Participate in internal and external training programs related to AML/CFT and other subjects that may form part of the day to day work requirements.

### Requirements:

- At least 3+ years’ directly related experience in a compliance role with a substantial knowledge of relevant rules and regulations and the day-to-day compliance affairs;
- Strong experience in corporate onboarding and different corporate structure types;
- Demonstrated ability to write effectively;
- Superior organizational skills;
- Strong communication skills;
- ACAMS desirable.

**Why Binance**

• Shape the future with the world’s leading blockchain ecosystem

• Collaborate with world-class talent in a user-centric global organization with a flat structure

• Tackle unique, fast-paced projects with autonomy in an innovative environment

• Thrive in a results-driven workplace with opportunities for career growth and continuous learning

• Competitive salary and company benefits

• Work-from-home arrangement (the arrangement may vary depending on the work nature of the business team)

Binance is committed to being an equal opportunity employer. We believe that having a diverse workforce is fundamental to our success.

*By submitting a job application, you confirm that you have read and agree to our* ***Candidate Privacy Notice****.*

Business analyst (fintech) [2508]

3-5 years of experience  • Full-time, Remote work  • English - Advanced (C1)  • Ukrainian - Native

We are looking for an experienced and proactive **Business analyst** to join our team at Dataforest and lead a long-term, high-scale FinTech project.

About the Project:

Our client is building a powerful B2B SaaS platform designed to revolutionize chargeback management, featuring enterprise-grade API integrations (Ethoca, Verifi), seamless payment processor connections (Stripe, Shopify, Braintree), and real-time dispute alerts. We are actively developing and scaling multiple product streams, including Business Health, Dispute Management, and others.

**You’ll be a great fit if you have:**

- 5+ years of experience in system, functional, or business analysis;

- English: Advanced and higher;

- Deep expertise in key business analysis techniques, requirement management tools, and standardizing BA documentation;

- Solid understanding of SDLC and Agile development processes;

- Strong hands-on experience in business process modeling (BPMN, UML) and domain-driven design;

- Proven proficiency in driving Discovery phases, extracting high-level business vision, and translating it into actionable roadmaps and specs;

- Advanced skills in drafting business (BRD), functional (SRS), and technical requirement specifications;

- Extensive experience in working with key business stakeholders and C-level executives, leading requirement elicitation and facilitation sessions;

- Exceptional critical thinking, problem-solving, and conflict-resolution skills;

- Ability to independently decompose complex system workflows and domain logic into manageable tasks;

- Strong technical background with a clear understanding of web development concepts, enterprise system integrations, and API design;

**- Practical experience using modern AI tools (ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot, etc.) to accelerate requirement generation, documentation, and analysis workflows.**

**Would be a plus:**

- Prior experience in FinTech, PayTech, Chargeback, or Payments domain;

- Experience working with projects that integrate AI/ML features or LLM API solutions;

- Hands-on experience with SQL and data modeling;

- Experience with integration-heavy B2B SaaS projects and payment gateway APIs (e.g., Stripe, Braintree).

**What you’ll do:**

- Serving as the primary point of contact for stakeholders to elicit, clarify, and validate complex product requirements;

- Leading the end-to-end requirement lifecycle: from high-level discovery down to backlog grooming, user story mapping, and detailing acceptance criteria;

- Visualizing complex FinTech workflows, business processes, and data models for multi-stream engineering teams;

- Advising stakeholders on industry best practices, platform capabilities, and optimal product solutions;

- Performing market research and domain analysis to contribute to product strategy and features elaboration;

- Communicating project vision and closely aligning requirements with System Architects, Tech Leads, and engineering teams;

- Actively participating in presale estimations, discovery activities, and scope definition for new product streams;

**- Drive & improve AI-driven BA practices: Leverage AI tools to speed up requirement drafting, analyze complex domain data, optimize BA artifacts, and enhance delivery processes.**

**We ensure your growth with:**

- Opportunity to work with the high-skilled engineering team on challenging projects;

- Interesting projects with new technologies;

- Great networking opportunities with international clients, challenging tasks;

- Building interesting projects from scratch using new technologies;

- Personal and professional development opportunities;

- Competitive salary fixed in USD;

- Paid vacation and sick leaves;

- Flexible work schedule;

- Friendly working environment with minimal hierarchy;

- Team building activities, corporate events.

**Purpose of Job**

The Analyst is a member of the Gender and Economic Inclusion Team (G&EI) which consists of three pillars (Access to Skills and Employment, Access to Finance and Entrepreneurship, and Access to Services) and plays an important role in implementing the Bank’s mandate to promote transition in the EBRD’s countries of operations (COOs). Under the overall guidance of the Director, Gender and Economic Inclusion, the post holder will work with the WE Finance Code Lead to coordinate the gender and inclusion actions related to the implementation of the WE Finance Code and cooperate with the WeFinance Code Lead and relevant colleagues on overall operationalization of the cross-regional programme. 

The WE Finance Code is a global policy initiative, funded by We-Fi, that aims to close financing barriers faced by women entrepreneurs through a coordinated public-private stakeholder effort to improve collection and use of sex-disaggregated data. The post holder will support and coordinate the ongoing We-Fi activities across all three regions, with special focus on activities in Egypt and Morocco. Specifically, with the support of the WE Finance Code Lead, the Analyst will coordinate as required the rollout of all steps envisioned for the implementation of the WE Finance Code. They will oversee technical assistance projects and the work of the WE Finance Code implementing consultant in the regions. Moreover, sitting in HQ, the post holder will support the WE Finance Code lead with overall operationalisation and coordination of the cross-regional WE Finance Code Programme. The analyst will oversee and track the programme budget, ensuring compliance with internal EBRD policies and donor funds agreements. They will also engage on reporting to the donor and other stakeholders, tracking progress and identifying lessons learned from the region. 

The post holder will work in close cooperation with G&EI colleagues as well as other departments under the VP3 (i.e. Climate Strategy and Delivery (CSD), Policy Strategy and Delivery (PSD), Impact & Partnerships (IP)), the Banking department and other Bank groups (Risk, Environmental and Social Teams, Legal), Communications, and with Resident Offices (Ros). 

**Background**

The GEI department falls under the Vice Presidency for Policy and Partnerships (VP3) which has an ambitious vision for the Bank’s policy, partnerships and impact agenda. The VP3 aims to: (i) streamline the Bank’s policy agenda by centralising the policy coordination and delivery functions; (ii) improve the Bank’s results, knowledge and learning architecture and (iii) enhance the objectivity, rigor, credibility and accountability of the Bank’s Impact function. The vision for this change is to have a more strategic, coherent, focused and better aligned policy, impact and partnerships functions fit for purpose to deliver on the ever more complex challenges faced by our COOs.  

Under the VP3, the GEI Department leads the design and implementation of the EBRD’s Strategy for the Promotion of Gender Equality (SPGE 2021-2025) and the Equality of Opportunity Strategy (EOS 2021-2025). The Department also leads on the operationalisation of the engagement areas of the 2 strategies at project/ policy levels, regular internal/external updates. The Department also leads project, policy and TC design and delivery of products/solutions for access to entrepreneurship and finance, skills and jobs, and services, and inclusive elements of digital and green project/policy engagement across regions/sectors, in partnership with banking. Manage the design and implementation of the gender SMART tagging process across all sectors, provide advice to banking on optimising gender impact, and track progress. Create gender/inclusive knowledge products; lead international/MDB engagement in these areas.

**Facts / Scale**

* The post holder is part of the Access to Finance and Entrepreneurship pillar of the Gender & Economic Inclusion team in PSD. (They report to the Associate Director, G&EI, and supports the team and the G&EI Director on cross-pillar initiatives and products;
* The post holder will further be recognised in the gender and inclusion field with specific focus on access to finance and entrepreneurship with the youth and regional inclusion, migration and refugees, skills development, inclusive finance, and works across thematic teams within G&EI;
* The post holder works with and supports the WE Finance Code Lead
* The post holder supports the implementation of one large-scale inclusion and gender policy engagement programme, in particular the WE Finance Code, and interacts with the relevant Banking colleagues in HQs and relevant ROs, and external stakeholders as needed, in Egypt and Morocco
* The post holder supports implementation of at least 3 technical assistance assignments related to the WE Finance Code, including project and policy level activities, the successful management of consultants, the delivery of outputs on time and to budget, as well as related donor engagement, reporting and, at times, fundraising.
* The post holder tracks the We Finance programme budget, obtains internal approvals when needed, ensuring compliance with EBRD policies and donor agreements.
* The post holder provides key input and oversight of inclusion and gender policy elements into country diagnostic studies and country strategies and engages with EPG Regional Lead Economists, the Country Strategy teams in HQ and other key EBRD teams on inclusion elements of country strategies.
* The post holder contributes to selected G&EI management issues as required.
* The post holder acts as a champion and role model of the Bank’s Behavioural Competencies and Corporate Behaviours, ensuring adherence within the team(s) so that the highest standards of integrity and ethical conduct are always exhibited.
* No budget responsibility.

**Accountabilities & Responsibilities**

* In line with the Bank’s Transition mandate, supports the design, appraisal and monitoring of investment projects and TCs for their impact on inclusion as part of transition and monitors the portfolio of projects with inclusion impact for transition performance, through engagement with Banking project teams and due diligence visits to the region.
* Supports the implementation of the policy dialogue activities under WE Finance Code engaging with the relevant ecosystem players and champions at the national, regional, and international levels. This will include supporting the national and regional coalitions, supporting signatories, and tracking progress.
* Manages Technical Cooperation (TC) projects related to the WE Finance Code, supports the selection of consultants when needed, oversees the work of the Code implementing consultants in the region, tracks their progress, and ensures outputs are delivers on time and on budget.
* Supports the We Finance Code Lead on overall programme management. Tracks the We Finance programme budget, obtaining internal approvals when needed, tracks overall programme progress and engages in donor reporting, and provides administrative support to manage consultancy contracts.
* Monitors and assesses reform challenges and progress in relation to inclusion and gender issues in SEMED, and support the We Finance Code lead on the design and delivery of gender-responsive policy dialogue, through analytical work, contributions towards strategy papers and supports liaising with key senior level stakeholders such as banking regulator, banking associations, credit guarantees and information bureaus, private sector clients and strategic partners of the Bank.
* Supports inclusion and gender capacity building within the Bank, specifically in Banking teams and Regional / Resident Offices, through presentations, inclusion and gender workshops and seminars. Maintains a strong awareness of the international debate on gender, inclusion, skills and inequality issue.
* Support with the organisation of events to promote the launch, awareness, and visibility of the Code. Attends events and represents EBRD as needed (e.g., at workshops, events, dialogues with stakeholders).
* Creates and co-creates the knowledge tools and guidance notes for internal and external consumption including through tailor-made surveys and established EBRD’s publications (especially donor funded ones) and channels to promote the promotion of equality of opportunity strategic priority of the Bank across its policy engagements, investments and advisory services.
* Contributes to joint work across departments and across pillars as needed.

**Knowledge, Skills, Experience & Qualifications**

* A postgraduate degree in economics, international development or related field.
* Demonstrated policy or development / inclusion / gender expertise and prior work experience in policy oriented or development area, gained for example through full-time employment in a financial or governmental institution, consultancy/company, think tank or academia;
* Substantial progressive responsibility mainstreaming gender and inclusion in projects in international organizations in a variety of sector with experience in supporting private and public sector;
* Strong social analysis and research skills including command of quantitative and qualitative methods of research, and knowledge of gender and inclusion issues in a variety or regions;
* Knowledge and experience applying results-based approaches to project and program management;
* Experience of working with donors and familiarity with broader donor debates and best practices;
* Fieldwork experience in EBRD countries of operations will be considered an advantage;
* Ability to think strategically, and to innovate, results oriented, ability to work under several deadlines simultaneously;
* Good interpersonal skills;
* Ability to work in a multicultural team;
* Excellent oral and writing skills in English;

