# Model Risk Management Senior Analyst

## Job Introduction



Handelsbanken is a relationship bank built on trust, long-term thinking and local decision-making. We provide bespoke banking and wealth management services to personal and corporate customers,

Our decentralised model means decisions are made close to the customer, in our branches. Our central Functions teams play a vital role in supporting the branch network, providing the expertise, governance and infrastructure that enable branches to serve customers effectively and sustainably.

This approach had underpinned our success for decades. Handelsbanken is independently recognised as one of Europe’s safest commercial banks, holds the strongest credit rating among its peers and is consistently ranked highly for customer satisfaction and relationship banking.

Our culture is values-led, shaped by trust, respect, and long-term thinking. We empower our people to use their expertise, make confident decisions and build long-term careers. We look for people who share our long- term vision, want to grow and want to make a meaningful impact in their local community and with the Bank

We also recognise that flexibility can support people to perform at their best, and that it looks different for everyone. While arrangements will depend on the requirements of the role and the needs of the business, we are open to having a conversation around what flexibility could look like for you.

Check our **Handelsbanken website** for further information

**The opportunity** 

We are looking for a Model Risk Management Senior Analyst to join the Bank.

The Model Risk Management (MRM) team sits within the UKR Risk department and is responsible for the design and maintenance of the Bank's Model Risk Management framework, ensuring robust model governance, independent challenge and effective oversight of models across the Bank.

As the Bank continues its deliberate and disciplined adoption of Artificial Intelligence (AI), the MRM team is expanding its remit to provide independent validation, challenge and governance of AI systems and AI-enabled use cases. The Bank does not seek to be a first mover in AI technologies; instead, it aims to adopt and scale AI capabilities where benefits can be clearly demonstrated and where appropriate governance, controls and oversight mechanisms are in place.

This role offers a unique opportunity to join the Bank at an early stage of its AI journey and contribute to the development and embedding of the Bank's AI Model Risk Management Framework. The successful candidate will support the independent review, validation and ongoing oversight of AI systems and use cases, including Generative AI (GenAI), Large Language Models (LLMs), Agentic AI solutions and third-party AI-enabled applications.

The role will be responsible for ensuring that AI-related risks are appropriately identified, assessed, documented, challenged and monitored throughout the lifecycle of AI use cases, in line with the Bank's risk appetite, governance standards and regulatory expectations, including PRA SS1/23.

**Key responsibilities**

* Perform independent reviews, validations and risk assessments of AI systems, AI-enabled use cases and existing models, providing objective challenge and oversight;
* Support the implementation and ongoing enhancement of the Bank's AI Model Risk Management Framework, Validation Standards and associated governance processes;
* Assess whether key AI risks have been appropriately identified, documented, mitigated and monitored throughout the lifecycle of AI use cases;
* Support the identification, registration, validation and ongoing monitoring of in-scope AI systems and use cases;
* Contribute to the development and maintenance of a risk-based AI Risk Rating methodology to support proportionate oversight and governance;
* Maintain the Bank's AI Use Case Inventory, ensuring it remains accurate, complete and up to date;
* Prepare validation findings, risk assessments and recommendations for presentation to relevant governance forums, including the Model Oversight Committee (MOC);
* Engage with stakeholders across Risk, Technology, Information Security, Data Governance, Compliance, Legal and Change functions to support effective AI governance and oversight;
* Monitor regulatory developments and industry best practice relating to model risk management and AI governance, supporting the continuous enhancement of Bank frameworks and standards.

**What we’re looking for**

Research (by Harvard University) shows that women are particularly likely to second guess themselves and not apply - so if you are worried you don't meet all the criteria, get in touch anyhow and let us do the worrying...

* Experience in model risk management, quantitative risk, validation, analytics, technology risk, data science or a related discipline within financial services;
* Experience reviewing, validating or providing oversight of quantitative models, analytical tools, risk methodologies or technology-enabled solutions;
* An understanding of model risk management principles and regulatory expectations, including familiarity with PRA SS1/23 or equivalent guidance;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify key risks, challenge assumptions and provide independent judgement;
* An interest in Artificial Intelligence, Generative AI and emerging technologies, and an appreciation of the opportunities and risks they present within a regulated environment;
* Understanding of key AI risk themes, such as transparency, bias, explainability, governance, data quality, privacy, security and human oversight;
* Experience using data analysis or programming tools such as Python, SQL, R or similar technologies;
* Ability to understand and assess complex technical concepts, even where direct subject matter expertise may not exist;
* Strong communication and report-writing skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts and validation findings to both technical and non-technical audiences;
* A naturally curious mindset, strong attention to detail and a desire to learn, challenge and contribute to the safe and responsible adoption of AI.

**Why join Handelsbanken**

We want everyone at Handelsbanken to feel supported, motivated, and able to do great work. That’s why, alongside brilliant colleagues, meaningful work and training and development opportunities, we provide a variety of benefits designed with your wellbeing in mind. 

In addition, there is a flexible benefits package with the key highlights detailed below.



**Application next steps** 

Your journey with us begins once you have submitted your application. One of our Handelsbanken Talent Acquisition Partners will be reviewing your details and will later organise a phone conversation if your experience aligns with our requirements, we will extend an invitation for you to participate in an interview.  

*This advert will be live for a minimum of two weeks. However, please note that after the two weeks, the closing date could change at any time depending on the number of responses received.*

*The Bank is deeply committed to embedding good equality and diversity practice into all of our activities. This is so that we are an inclusive, welcoming and inspiring place to work that encourages everyone to apply, regardless of socio-economic background, age, disability, pregnancy and/or parental status, race (including colour, nationality, and ethnic or national origin), veteran status, marital and civil partnership status, religion or belief, sex, gender reassignment or sexual orientation.*

#LI-JT1 #LI-Hybrid

**Job title:** Regional Manager - Ireland

**Location:** Field based – Northern Ireland

We are looking for a Regional Manager to cover both the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland, based in one of those locations. **Please apply for this position only if you are available/interested in being based in the Northern Ireland location.**

**Why Join HSB?**

We don’t just inspect—we protect. At HSB, you’ll join a team with a clear purpose, strong values, and a supportive culture where your expertise is respected and your contributions matter. From flexible working to wellbeing support, we invest in you so you can bring your best self to work—every day.

Apply today and become part of a company that doesn’t just engineer safety—but inspires trust.

**What You’ll Be Doing**

As a Regional Manager, you will lead a team of Engineering Surveyors across the Republic of Ireland and Northern Ireland, ensuring the delivery of exceptional customer service, operational excellence, and regulatory compliance. You'll work closely with Operations Managers and Technical Teams to ensure contractual commitments are achieved while creating an engaged, motivated, and high-performing workforce. You will be responsible for resource planning, performance management, recruitment activities, customer satisfaction, financial performance, and maintaining the highest standards of safety and service delivery within your region.

**What Makes This Role Special**

* Leadership impact: Lead and inspire a team of engineering professionals who make a difference every day;
* Business ownership: Take full responsibility for the operational and financial performance of your region, including P&L accountability;
* Growth opportunity: Play a key role in supporting business growth ambitions across Ireland while developing your own career;
* Field-based leadership: Work closely with your team in the field, providing coaching, support, and visible leadership;
* Trusted brand: Join a business recognised for technical excellence, customer service, and innovation as part of the wider Munich Re Group.

**What You Bring**

* Proven leadership experience managing field-based engineering or service delivery teams;
* Strong people management skills with the ability to motivate, coach, and develop high-performing teams;
* Excellent stakeholder and customer relationship management capabilities;
* Strong commercial awareness with experience managing budgets, performance metrics, and business objectives;
* Excellent planning and organisational skills, with the ability to effectively balance resources and workloads;
* A confident and proactive approach with a strong focus on results and continuous improvement;
* Commitment to maintaining and promoting a positive safety culture.

**What You’ll Need**

* Demonstrable experience leading field-based engineering or service-oriented teams;
* Engineering qualification;
* GCSE Maths and English (or equivalent);
* Strong understanding of KPI management and operational performance delivery;
* Knowledge of regulations including LOLER, PSSR, PUWER, COSHH, and Safety, Health and Welfare at Work Regulations would be advantageous;
* Previous experience within engineering inspection, lifting equipment, pressure systems, LEV systems, power presses, or related engineering disciplines would be advantageous;
* Holder of a full UK or Irish driving licence with no more than 6 penalty points.

**What We Offer**

In addition to a competitive salary and excellent work-life balance, you'll benefit from an industry-leading rewards package:

* 25 days Annual Leave + Bank Holidays + 2 Well-being days each year
* Ability to buy or sell leave.
* Up to 13% Pension contribution (9% non-contributory plus up to 4% matching contribution).
* Eligibility for an Annual Bonus up to 15% (dependent on Group performance)
* Private Medical & Dental (options to add family members at discounted rates)
* Life Assurance of six times salary
* Wellbeing and Development Scheme + EAP + Health Assessments (subject to scheme eligibility)
* Study & continuing Professional Development Support
* Choice of company vehicle or car allowance
* Access to Salary Sacrifice Car scheme
* Access to a range of discounted benefits such as critical illness cover and mortgage advisory services.

**Diversity, Equity & Inclusion**

At HSB, Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion foster innovation and resilience and enable us to act braver and better. Embracing the power of DEI is at the core of who we are. We recognise diversity can be multi-dimensional, intersectional, and complex, so we want to build a diverse workforce that includes a wide range of racial, ethnic, sexual, and gender identities; economic and geographic backgrounds; physical abilities; ages; life, school, and career experiences; and political, religious, and personal beliefs. Additionally, we are committed to building an equitable and inclusive work environment where this diversity is celebrated, valued, and has equitable opportunities to succeed.

All candidates in consideration for any role can request a reasonable adjustment at any point in our recruitment process. You can request an adjustment by speaking to your Talent Acquisition contact.

# Senior Product Designer

**About Sedex**

Sedex is a trusted partner for over 100,000 businesses worldwide, helping them create **socially and environmentally sustainable supply chains**. Through our platform's powerful data insights and expert guidance, we simplify the management, assessment, and reporting of sustainability performance.

Our Vision is to be a leader in making global supply chains more socially and environmentally sustainable. Our Mission is To provide data-driven insights, accessible tools, and exceptional services that support businesses in improving environmental, social, and governance (ESG) performance and outcomes.

**The role**

Our Product, Design and Technology department is looking for a Senior Product Designer to join our team and play a key role in crafting the Sedex product experience.

Working as part of the wider Product Design team, you will operate within a multi-disciplinary squad dedicated to one of our core revenue streams. This is an ideal opportunity for someone seeking to hone their development in both user experience and interface design.

Our platform is used by buyer and supplier organisations – you will work across the supplier side and be involved in all areas of the product development lifecycle, from discovery and validation to delivery of key new features. Additionally, you will be expected to document and own the end-to-end journey map for suppliers, identifying issues and working with stakeholders to prioritise fixing them.

**Key Responsibilities**

As a Senior Product Designer you will:

* Work closely with Product, Engineering, Delivery and Analytics to support our supplier platform;

* Assist in defining, refining and prioritising user needs and business requirements, translating them both into design tasks;

* Document and own the end-to-end journey for supplier organisations, using data to surface real world user issues for prioritisation on our roadmap;

* Participate in user research activities and assist in interpreting the results into usable product feedback;

* Gather analysis on competing products and features to inform user experience decisions;

* Ideate, sketch, wireframe and prototype product features and components;

* Provide high-fidelity user interface designs using components that can help inform our design system;

* Lead conversations with business stakeholders from outside the Product, Design and Technology department;

* Liaise directly with Front and Back End Engineers throughout the design process;

* Be responsible for design sign off for components, and features, before they go live;

* Identify opportunities to use emerging technologies, including AI, to improve design processes, increase efficiency and create better customer outcomes; and

* Participate in recruitment of other Product Designers.

**Knowledge, Skills & Experience**

As a member of the Product Design team you will ideally have:

* A willingness and desire to improve your Product Design skillset;
* A great portfolio that demonstrates how you approach and solve Product Design problems;

* Experience producing tactical and strategic design outputs;

* A good appreciation of the role qualitative and quantitative user research plays in Product Design, and when to use either;

* A good understanding of user experience design, behavioural design and usability concepts;

* A solid comprehension of the practical applications of design principles, including grid, typography, and colour theory;

* A good understanding of interaction design and design systems;

* An advanced knowledge of the accessibility implications of Product Design decisions;

* Great time management and workload prioritisation skills;

* An understanding of Front and Back End technologies and how they impact design considerations;

* A collaborative attitude, showing humility and empathy when dealing with others;

* The ability to give, and receive, constructive feedback;

* Excellent communication skills, whether written or verbal;

* Experience managing and influencing stakeholders;

* Some experience recruiting other Product Designers;

* An interest in keeping up to date with design trends and technology developments;
* Familiarity with AI tools and how they can positively impact design processes;

* Excellent Figma, or similar design software skills; and

* A relevant degree, equivalent qualification, or experience.

**Our culture**

At Sedex, our approach to business and culture is firmly rooted in our core values, which guide everything we do:

· **Respect Each Other**: We believe that a foundation of mutual respect is essential to creating a positive and inclusive environment.

· **Customer-Driven**: We are passionate about delivering exceptional value to our customers. By listening to their needs, understanding their challenges, and continuously adapting our solutions, we aim to empower them to achieve their sustainability goals and drive positive change in their supply chains.

· **Thinking Creatively**: Innovation is at the heart of our work. We encourage creative problem-solving and embrace new ideas that challenge the status quo. This mindset allows us to continuously improve our products and services, offering fresh and effective solutions to complex sustainability and ethical sourcing issues.

· **Take Ownership**: We empower our team members to take responsibility for their actions and outcomes. Every person at Sedex is encouraged to own their work, make decisions with confidence, and contribute proactively to the success of the team and the business.

· **Deliver Results**: We are results-oriented and committed to delivering tangible, impactful outcomes for our customers, our business, and society at large.

# Senior Commercial Fleet Administrator

STRABAG UK are seeking an organised and driven Senior Commercial Fleet Administrator to provide support within our ever growing fleet team based at either our London headquarters or Wilton site in Redcar.

#### 

* Team working.&nbsp;
* Ability to encourage and develop a culture of commercial awareness within the team.&nbsp;
* Ability to provide support, guidance and coaching to junior staff on commercial matters.&nbsp;
* Strong customer service orientation and stakeholder focus.&nbsp;
* Strong organisational skills with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail in record keeping and administration.&nbsp;
* Effective written and verbal communication skills.

STRABAG - Work On Progress: Becoming Climate Neutral by 2040.

#### 

* Provide assistance commercial issues within the project(s).&nbsp;
* Assist in the preparation of internal commercial reporting and any other reports as required.&nbsp;
* Assist in the preparation of Valuations / Applications for Payment, including all supporting documentation in accordance with the contract.&nbsp;
* Identify commercial risks, opportunities, value engineering initiatives and change.&nbsp;
* Assist in cost control and cost mitigation activities.&nbsp;
* Apply cost allocation and coding structures in line with internal and external requirements.&nbsp;
* Provide cost reports as required.
* Input and post invoices&nbsp;
* Verify and process invoices against purchase order prices and delivered quantities.&nbsp;
* Match purchase orders and delivery notes with invoices.&nbsp;
