**Design Engineer Graduate**

**Description**

**About Us**

Textron Specialized Vehicles are a global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, side-by-sides, all-terrain vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment.

At Ransomes Jacobsen Ltd, we design and manufacture professional turf-care equipment under the brands of Ransomes and Jacobsen. Our mission is to be the premier supplier of high-quality and environmentally conscious turf equipment, providing superior performance for our customers. From prestigious championship golf courses to the World Cup, for more than a century, the most important turf in the world has been manicured by our brand.

**About the Role**

This is a full-time role based at our manufacturing facility in Ipswich, Suffolk.

As a Design Engineer I, you will support the delivery of high-quality mechanical design work across a range of projects. Working under the guidance of senior-engineering staff, you will contribute to the development of reliable, cost-effective, and manufacturable solutions that meet performance targets and regulatory requirements.

Your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

* Produce mechanical designs that meet defined technical, performance, reliability, and cost requirements;
* Create and maintain accurate engineering documentation, including drawings, Bills of Materials (BOMs), assembly instructions, and supporting technical publications in line with the Engineering Change process;
* Apply best-practice design principles and utilise in-house standards, approved reference materials, and standard components wherever appropriate;
* Ensure all designs are practical, efficient, and cost-effective to manufacture by working closely with Manufacturing and Production teams;
* Ensure designs are developed in context, maintaining compatibility with adjacent components, assemblies, and wider system architectures;
* Perform component-level CAE/FEA analyses to support design decisions, verify performance, and identify opportunities for improvement;
* Integrate mistake-proofing, clear visual guidance, or simplified features into designs to reduce the potential for assembly errors or rework;
* Collaborate with other Engineers and internal departments when implementing new design concepts or engineering approaches;
* Interpret and incorporate relevant industry standards, directives, and regulatory requirements into product designs;
* Support the engineering team in ensuring all documentation and designs comply with applicable quality and safety expectations;
* Assist in the development of test plans and validation activities to ensure key design elements and performance objectives are met;
* Support testing activities as required, including preparing test articles, reviewing results, and contributing to design refinements.

**Qualifications**

**About You**

As a Design Engineer I, we would ask you bring the following skills and experience:

* Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in an Engineering discipline, ideally Mechanical Engineering.
* Experience designing with a range of materials, including steels, plastics and alloys.
* Exposure to engineering development processes such as prototyping, testing, or design-for-manufacture desirable.
* Knowledge of DFME and PFMEA.
* Proficiency in CAD software (NX preferred) required.
* Familiarity with FEA tools, ideally ANSYS, to support basic analysis and validation activities.
* Hands-on approach, with the ability to work effectively within a multidisciplinary team to take design concepts through to medium-volume production.
* Self-motivated, capable of working independently toward defined objectives with minimal supervision.
* Strong attention to detail, with proven problem-solving skills and a methodical approach to engineering tasks.
* An interest in expanding knowledge across wider mechanical engineering disciplines as part of professional development.

**Why us?**

* Work life balance promoted with every other Friday off;
* 30 days annual leave;
* Competitive rate of pay, reviewed annually;
* Enhanced Company pension;
* Life assurance of four times your annual salary;
* Comprehensive Employee Assistance Program for you and your immediate family;
* Access to Textron University’s self-service training platform;
* Eye care scheme;
* Discounts on gym memberships, shopping and travel through Perks at Work;
* Onsite golf course and football pitch;
* Winter flu vaccination voucher.

**Senior Design Engineer**

**Description**

Textron Specialized Vehicles Inc. is a leading global manufacturer of golf cars, utility and personal transportation vehicles, professional turf-care equipment, and ground support equipment. Textron Specialized Vehicles markets products under several different brands. Its vehicles are found in environments ranging from golf courses to factories, airports to planned communities, and theme parks to hunting preserves.

As a Design Engineer III, you will lead the development of high-quality mechanical design solutions across a range of projects. You will independently manage complex engineering activities, applying advanced technical knowledge to deliver reliable, cost-effective and manufacturable products that meet performance, quality and regulatory requirements. In addition, you will provide technical leadership, mentor less experienced engineers and contribute to the continuous improvement of engineering capability and product performance.

Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:

* Lead the design and development of complex mechanical systems and products, ensuring technical, performance, reliability, manufacturability, and cost requirements are achieved throughout the product lifecycle;
* Take ownership of significant engineering projects and workstreams, providing technical direction and ensuring design activities are delivered to agreed quality, cost, and timing objectives;
* Create, review, approve and maintain engineering documentation, including drawings, Bills of Materials (BOMs), assembly instructions and technical publications, ensuring compliance with Engineering Change processes and engineering standards;
* Establish and promote best practice engineering methods, standards and design principles, driving consistency and continual improvement across the Engineering team;
* Ensure designs are robustly integrated within wider production architectures, considering system interactions, serviceability, manufacturing requirements, reliability and customer needs;
* Lead advanced CAE/FEA analyses and engineering calculations to validate design concepts, optimize performance and reduce technical risk;
* Drive Design for Manufacture (DFM), Design for Assembly (DFA), Design for Reliability (DFR) and cost-reduction initiatives through close collaboration with Manufacturing, Quality, Supply Chain and Production teams;
* Identify technical risks, conduct root cause investigations and develop effective engineering solutions to resolve complex product or manufacturing issues;
* Lead design reviews and provide technical guidance, challenge and approval of engineering solutions developed by other engineers;
* Interpret, apply and advise on relevant legislation, standards, directives and regulatory requirements, ensuring product compliance across applicable markets;
* Plan, define and lead validation and verification activities, including test strategy development, test execution reviews and technical sign-off of results;
* Mentor and develop junior engineers, providing coaching, technical support and knowledge sharing to strengthen overall engineering capability;
* Collaborate with cross-functional and international teams to develop new technologies, products and engineering approaches aligned with business strategy;
* Support product roadmap and technology planning activities by identifying opportunities for innovation, product improvement and competitive advantage.

**Qualifications**

* Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in an Engineering discipline, ideally Mechanical Engineering.
* At least five years’ experience in mechanical design and product development within a manufacturing environment, including responsibility for leading projects from concept through to production release.
* Proven experience designing with a range of materials, including steels, plastics, alloys and fabricated assemblies.
* Strong understanding of engineering development processes including prototyping, testing, design-for-manufacture (DFM), design for assembly (DFA) and product validation.
* Advanced knowledge and practical application of DFMEA and PFMEA methodologies.
* Experience leading design reviews and collaborating across Engineering, Manufacturing, Quality and Supply Chain functions to resolve complex technical and product performance issues.
* Advanced proficiency in CAD software (NX preferred), including complex assemblies, system integration and engineering documentation.
* Proficiency in FEA tools, ideally ANSYS, with the ability to perform and interpret analyses to support design verification, optimisation and decision-making.
* Experience using PLM and ERP systems to manage engineering data, product structures and engineering change processes desirable.
* Hands-on approach, with the ability to lead multidisciplinary engineering activities and take products from concept through to production.
* Self-motivated and capable of leading complex engineering projects with minimal supervision.
* Strong technical leadership skills to mentor and support less experienced engineers.
* Excellent problem-solving skills, with a structured and methodical approach.
* Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence decisions across the organisation.
* High attention to detail and commitment to delivering robust, reliable and manufacturable engineering solutions.
* A continuous improvement mindset, with a desire to drive innovation and best practice.

# Principal Dams Engineer

Wallingford, UK

At HR Wallingford, we design smart, resilient solutions across the natural and built environments to help everyone live and work more sustainably with water. By harnessing research, data insights and the power of our collective expertise, we help the world to better understand the changing influence and impact of water.

HR Wallingford is not just a workplace; it's a community of exceptional minds pushing the boundaries of conventional thinking. As a not-for-profit company, our focus is on research, innovation, and developing our people, tools, and technology. Here, you'll have the freedom to make long-term decisions that sustain our colleagues, business, and environment.

We are recruiting for a Principal Dams Engineer within our thriving Water and Climate Division, where you will help shape the leadership of our ambitious Dams Sector team. Drawing upon your wealth of experience in the UK reservoir industry, you'll play a pivotal role in the intricate landscape of dam and reservoir engineering.

As a key contributor to our team, your expertise extends across several of the various domains relevant to this team, including hydrology, geotechnics, flood control, hydropower, water supply, risk assessment, and asset management. Collaborate with a diverse team of civil engineers, numerical modellers, and software developers, all committed to crafting innovative solutions for the most complex challenges in the field.

Beyond your core responsibilities, this role offers a unique opportunity to actively engage in, and even lead, ground-breaking research, and development projects. This not only adds depth to your professional journey but also fuels the growth of our business and the dam safety industry.

**Key qualifications and skills**

* A degree in civil engineering, hydrology, or geotechnical engineering;
* Current appointment to the Supervising Engineers Panel;
* Experience of working in the UK reservoir industry;
* Chartered Status (CEng);
* At least 10 years of professional experience related to dams and reservoirs;
* Knowledge of the UK Reservoirs Act 1975 and key industry guidance documents;
* Proven project management skills for studies, design or construction projects;
* An inquisitive nature and interest in leading research and development projects related to dam safety;
* Successful bid writing and business development experience;
* Experience of managing teams;
* Ability to work collaboratively with multi-disciplinary teams;
* Excellent inter-personal and client liaison skills;
* Excellent oral and written communication skills in English.

**Further information**

* Download a full job description and person specification.
* Check out our exceptional benefits at hrwallingford.com/careers.
* A salary from £51,000 - £70,000 dependant on experience
* We understand the importance of a healthy work-life balance and offer both hybrid working and flexi-time. We are also open to exploring other flexible working arrangements, including part-time.
* The closing date for applications is 31 October 2026.

**How to apply**

If you are excited about this role but unsure whether you’re the right fit, we encourage you to apply. We’re also happy to answer any questions by emailing careers@hrwallingford.com

Interested? Please apply providing your CV with covering letter.

